      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-21T00:58:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Unless you've got a link where Christopher gives the official definition of \"look at\", then that's not helping. :)</p><p>When you reveal a card, is it still the top card on the deck or does the unrevealed one beneath it become the top card? &nbsp;If all you're doing is looking at it and replacing it, then how can you \"reveal cards until you find XYZ\"? &nbsp;That one revealed card will always be the top card of the deck - you'll never get any deeper.</p><p>Do you have to show it to everyone or can you keep the information to yourself (I know it's a coop game, but it's a legit question).</p><p>I don't have any trouble figuring out what \"reveal\" means, but if I'm going to put it in the FAQ, I figure there should be a well-reasoned, official answer.</p>",
      "post_number": 3,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:08:22.641Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
