      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Unless you&#39;ve got a link where Christopher gives the official definition of &quot;look at&quot;, then that&#39;s not helping. :)</p><p>When you reveal a card, is it still the top card on the deck or does the unrevealed one beneath it become the top card? &nbsp;If all you&#39;re doing is looking at it and replacing it, then how can you &quot;reveal cards until you find XYZ&quot;? &nbsp;That one revealed card will always be the top card of the deck - you&#39;ll never get any deeper.</p><p>Do you have to show it to everyone or can you keep the information to yourself (I know it&#39;s a coop game, but it&#39;s a legit question).</p><p>I don&#39;t have any trouble figuring out what &quot;reveal&quot; means, but if I&#39;m going to put it in the FAQ, I figure there should be a well-reasoned, official answer.</p>",
