      "created_at": "2015-02-21T05:05:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p><span class=\"bbcode-s\">I don't have the exact quote, but</span> I'm sure that MigrantP has said somewhere that revealed cards go into their own special zone, and as such are not considered in the deck while they are revealed. &nbsp;Give me a moment to see if I can dig up the quote.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>EDIT: &nbsp;<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/97229#comment-97229\" data-bbcode=\"true\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Got it!</a></p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>AlexxKay is correct. In the digital version those cards would be in Parse's Revealed location, which is just another location like Deck, Trash, Hand, or InPlay.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:08:22.708Z",
