    {
      "id": 132827,
      "name": "bluedarky",
      "username": "bluedarky",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/bluedarky/{size}/1975_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-21T05:14:14.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Migrant P has commented in the past that revealed cards in the app get put into a special revealed card zone until they're put back into the deck or discarded.</p><p>We do know that revealing the top card of the deck removes it from the top due to Wraith and Visionary being able to set off Ambuscades traps with their scry cards as well.</p><p>So based on Migrant P's details of what happens in the app and the Ambuscade ruling the conclusion is that revealed cards are not on top of the deck anymore and the card underneath becomes the top card.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:08:22.795Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
