      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "[quote=\"Spiff\"]\n\nWhat you guys are saying makes perfect sense, but I&#39;m going to be a pedant about it anyway. Just because the app has a special zone for revealed cards doesn&#39;t mean that&#39;s officially how the card game works. I only want to put it in the FAQ if it&#39;s officially how the card game works.&nbsp;\n\n[/quote]\n\ncorrect me if i&#39;m wrong but doesn&#39;t your FAQ already have the ambuscade&#39;s trap ruling?\n\nAll cards that reveal (or look at) either put them on top or bottom of the deck, discard them, or shuffle them back into the deck, the trap ruling already states that cards leave the top of the deck when reveal ed as the trigger condition for the traps is to be the top card of the deck, but revealed cards don&#39;t enter play so must exist in a limbo like zone until one of the above things happen to them. \n\nOf course if revealed cards entered play it ups Progeny from a difficulty 4 to a 6.\n",
